{
  "id": "COMPOUND:19303 - PROTEIN:5032",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between Mansouramycin A and DMS-79, mediated through the CD70 antigen. This relationship is supported by multiple pathways, all of which converge on the CD70 antigen as a common target. Mansouramycin A directly interacts with CD70, which is then targeted by Garcinone B and Azelate, both of which ultimately lead to DMS-79. The high scores in all three paths indicate a consistent and robust relationship, suggesting that the CD70 antigen serves as a critical intermediate in the pathway from Mansouramycin A to DMS-79. The presence of multiple targets at the CD70 level, including Garcinone B and Azelate, implies that the CD70 antigen may be a key node in a broader network of interactions, potentially involving other molecules that modulate DMS-79. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Mansouramycin A exerts its biological effects through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately target DMS-79.",
